,"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\nSubjects:</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"92550395":{"pageid":92550395,"ns":6,"title":"File:Raptor quest - southwest Idaho (IA raptorquestsouth00unse).pdf","index":18,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":6260052,"width":1700,"height":2177,"pagecount":40,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Raptor_quest_-_southwest_Idaho_%28IA_raptorquestsouth00unse%29.pdf/page1-1280px-Raptor_quest_-_southwest_Idaho_%28IA_raptorquestsouth00unse%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1639,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Raptor_quest_-_southwest_Idaho_%28IA_raptorquestsouth00unse%29.pdf/page1-1280px-Raptor_quest_-_southwest_Idaho_%28IA_raptorquestsouth00unse%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1639},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Raptor_quest_-_southwest_Idaho_%28IA_raptorquestsouth00unse%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raptor_quest_-_southwest_Idaho_(IA_raptorquestsouth00unse).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=92550395","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<dl><dd>33 pages\u00a0: 28 cm</dd>\n<dd>\"This booklet takes you first on a self-guided tour of the World Center for Birds of Prey. Here you can explore the exhibits and see these exciting birds up close ... Then you're off on a field trip into the Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey National Conservation Area (NCA). There you will hike to the top of an old volcano and walk the rim of the Snake River Canyon. The NCA is a wonderful place to see birds of prey in the special raptor habitat that exists right here in southwest Idaho. To become a Junior Ranger, visit the places in this book. While you are there, complete the activities for that location\"--Page 1</dd>\n<dd>Hello, junior ranger -- Welcome to the World Center for Birds of Prey! -- Get ready to explore raptor habitat! -- Idaho raptor safari -- Initial point -- Dedication point -- Summary activities -- Junior ranger pledge -- Volunteer to help raptors</dd>\n<dd>Cover title</dd>\n<dd>\"Join the adventure.\"</dd>\n<dd>\"This publication was produced by the Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey National Conservation Area, with assistance from The Peregrine Fund\"--Page 2 of cover</dd>\n<dd>\"Publishing services by the BLM National Operations Center\"--Page 2 of cover</dd>\n<dd>Revision to the 2014 version</dd>\n<dd>\"BLM/ID/GI-14/003+8367+REV2016.\"</dd></dl>\n<br>Subjects: World Center for Birds of Prey; World Center for Birds of Prey; Public lands -- Study and teaching -- Activity programs; Public lands -- Idaho -- Juvenile literature; Birds of prey -- Study and teaching -- Activity programs -- Idaho; Birds of prey -- Idaho -- Juvenile literature; Nature observation -- Study and teaching -- Activity programs -- Idaho; Nature observation -- Idaho -- Juvenile literature; Activity programs in education; Birds of prey; Nature observation; Public lands; Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey National Conservation Area (Idaho); Idaho; Idaho -- Morley Nelson Snake River Birds of Prey National Conservation Area</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"93509256":{"pageid":93509256,"ns":6,"title":"File:Real children in many lands; a series of visits through the stereoscope (IA realchildreninma00emer).pdf","index":13,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":103290683,"width":1083,"height":1716,"pagecount":