ageid":91678933,"ns":6,"title":"File:The Grog Issue 47 (2018) (IA TheGrogIssue472018).pdf","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":23780519,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":44,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/The_Grog_Issue_47_%282018%29_%28IA_TheGrogIssue472018%29.pdf/page1-960px-The_Grog_Issue_47_%282018%29_%28IA_TheGrogIssue472018%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1656,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/The_Grog_Issue_47_%282018%29_%28IA_TheGrogIssue472018%29.pdf/page1-960px-The_Grog_Issue_47_%282018%29_%28IA_TheGrogIssue472018%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1656},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/The_Grog_Issue_47_%282018%29_%28IA_TheGrogIssue472018%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Grog_Issue_47_(2018)_(IA_TheGrogIssue472018).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=91678933","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nU.S. Navy. Bureau of Medicine and Surgery</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<div>Features<br>A Navy Nurse in Brazil................................................................page 4<br>by Cmdr. (ret.) Dymphna van Gorp, NC, USN<br>The Lebanon Crisis of 1958 and the Development of the<br>Navy Fleet Surgical Team Concept............................................page 12<br>Why a Navy Surgeon? Dr. Benjamin Rush Mitchell and the<br>Mexican War.................................................................................page 18<br>by James Alsop, PhD<br>The Story of \"CAPT Jack,\" Navy Surgeon:<br>Samoa, Magdalena Bay and Goat Island...................................page 24<br>by Bill Kaufman<br>Showcase<br>Dr. Rivers, the Rockefeller Institute and the Founding of<br>NAMRU-2.....................................................................................page 34<br>The Saga of Dr. John Doe, Marine Dentist...............................page 41<br>by LT Fred L. Losee, DC, USN<br></div><div><br></div><div>Introduction</div><br>In June 1943, the Army Air Force established the School of Air Evacuation at Bowman Field, Ky. to offer specialized training for its flight nurses. Among the first graduates of this school were two Navy<br>nurses--Dymphna van Gorp and Stephany Kozak. Van Gorp and Kozak would be instrumental in overseeing the development of the Navy's own aeromedical evacuation program as well as those of other nations. In<br><div>1944, these nurses travelled to South America to train the Brazilian Air Force's first flight nurses. In our cover story, Dymphna van Gorp offers a glimpse of this unique tour of duty.</div><div><br></div>Fleet Surgical Teams (FST) as we now know them today were the result of the Navy Medical Blue Ribbon Report of 1988. But the idea of deployable surgical units was nothing new in the Navy by 1988 and long<br><div>before there were FSTs, there were MTF-sponsored augmented surgical teams. In our second feature article we look back at the history of these teams and their early applications. <br></div><div><br></div><div>In his original article, \"Why a Navy Surgeon?,\"McMaster University's Dr. James Alsop examines the fascinating and peculiarcareer of Navy Surgeon Benjamin Rush Mitchell and his role in the Mexican War.</div><div><br></div><div>We follow these original stories with the next installment of the \"CAPT Jack\" chronicles, a history of the Naval Medical Research Unit No. 2, and look back at the experiences of a Navy dentist deployed with the\u00a0 Marines in the Pacific War in 1943. <br></div><div><br></div><div>As always, we hope you enjoy this tour on the high seas of Navy Medicine\u2019s past!</div><div><br></div><div>Editor and Historian:<br>Andr\u00e9 B. Sobocinski<br></div>\n<br>Subjects: history of medicine; Mexican-American War; NAMRU-2; World War II; dentistry</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"80476343":{"pageid":80476343,"ns":6,"title":"File:The Wikimedia Foundation's Heart of Knowledge Contest Magazine.pdf","index":20,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":4934275,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":27,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Wikimedia_Foundation%27s_Heart_of_Knowledge_Contest_Magazine.pdf/page1-960px-The_Wikimedia_Foundation%27s_Heart_of_Knowledge_Contest_Magazine.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1656,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Wikimedia_Foundation%27s_Heart_of_Knowledge_Contest_Magazine.pdf/page1-960px-The_Wikimedia_Foundation%27s_Heart_of_Knowledge_Contest_Magazine.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1656},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/The_Wikimedia_Foundation%27s_Heart_of_Knowledge_Contest_Magazine.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Wikimedia_Foundation%27s_Heart_of_Knowledge_Contest_Magazine.pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=80476343","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"In April 2019, the Wikimedia Foundation launched an international arts contest, called <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2019/03/28/announcing-the-heart-of-knowledge-contest-help-us-illustrate-why-knowledge-matters/\">Heart of Knowledge</a>, on the theme of open access to knowledge. Writers and artists around the world sent in submissions, and the winners are featured in this magazine.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Julia Whitty, Nanzi Muro, Opeyemi Owa, Ashley Ding, Jessica Shilling, Kathryn Garner, Elena Tatiana Chis, Jose Sender, Hina Husain, Hal Y. Zhang, Jonathan Qu, Wallace Kaufman, A. Molotkov, Teighlor McGee, Rafael Davis, Abhilash Jayachandra, Joshua Chalifour, Jennifer Sears, Hannah Cattanach, Sara Lynn Burnett","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"97766706":{"pageid":97766706,"ns":6,"title":"File:The two philosophers; a quaint, sad comedy (IA cu31924021995539).pdf","index":16,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":827533,"width":810,"height":1381,"pagecount":48,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/The_two_philosophers%3B_a_quaint%2C_sad_comedy_%28IA_cu31924021995539%29.pdf/page1-500px-The_two_philosophers%3B_a_quaint%2C_sad_comedy_%28IA_cu31924021995539%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":2182,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/The_two_philosophers%3B_a_quaint%2C_sad_comedy_%28IA_cu31924021995539%29.pdf/page1-500px-The_two_philosophers%3B_a_quaint%2C_sad_comedy_%28IA_cu31924021995539%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":2182},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/The_two_philosophers%3B_a_quaint%2C_sad_comedy_%28IA_cu31924021995539%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_two_philosophers;_a_quaint,_sad_comedy_(IA_cu31924021995539).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=97766706","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nChapman, John Jay, 1862-1933</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<p>The metadata below describe the original scanning. Follow the \"All Files: HTTP\" link in the \"View the book\" box to the left to find XML files that contain more metadata about the original images and the derived formats (OCR results, PDF etc.). See also the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/about/faqs.php#140\">What is the directory structure for the texts?</a> FAQ for information about file content and naming conventions.\n</p>\n<br>Subjects:</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"91392081":{"pageid":91392081,"ns":6,"title":"File:U.S. ASSISTANCE TO MICRONESIA AND THE MARSHALL ISLANDS- A QUESTION OF ACCOUNTABILITY (IA gov.gpo.fdsys.CHRG-106hhrg66709).pdf","index":19,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":3223487,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":103,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/U.S._ASSISTANCE_TO_MICRONESIA_AND_THE_MARSHALL_ISLANDS-_A_QUESTION_OF_ACCOUNTABILITY_%28IA_gov.gpo.fdsys.CHRG-106hhrg66709%29.pdf/page1-960px-U.S._ASSISTANCE_TO_MICRONESIA_AND_THE_MARSHALL_ISLANDS-_A_QUESTION_OF_ACCOUNTABILITY_%28IA_gov.gpo.fdsys.CHRG-106hhrg66709%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1656,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/U.S._ASSISTANCE_TO_MICRONESIA_AND_THE_MARSHALL_ISLANDS-_A_QUESTION_OF_ACCOUNTABILITY_%28IA_gov.gpo.fdsys.CHRG-106hhrg66709%29.pdf/page1-960px-U.S._ASSISTANCE_TO_MICRONESIA_AND_THE_MARSHALL_ISLANDS-_A_QUESTION_OF_ACCOUNTABILITY_%28IA_gov.gpo.fdsys.CHRG-106hhrg66